<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Consciousness Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 1960s–1980s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Black Consciousness Movement was a South African anti-apartheid movement of the late 1960s and 1970s led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steve-biko">Steve Biko</a> and others, beginning with the South African Students' Organisation in 1968. It urged black South Africans to reject white tutelage and build psychological and political self-reliance. Its ideas inspired the students of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soweto-uprising">Soweto uprising</a> of 1976, and its organisations were banned in 1977.</p></div>
